# Build context filter for api.Dockerfile. BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in
# preference to a .dockerignore at the context root, which is what lets this live beside the
# Dockerfile it belongs to instead of adding a repository-root file that both images would have
# to share. The build is still correct without it -- the `source` stage deletes node_modules
# itself -- but the context upload goes from megabytes to gigabytes.

# Secrets first. Nothing in this build reads them and no layer should be able to. The API image
# copies only dist and node_modules into the final stage, so a leaked .env would not reach the
# published image -- but it would reach the build cache and any intermediate stage that gets
# pushed, and a secret in a cache is still a secret you have to rotate.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
keypair*.json
wallet*.json

# Host installs and host builds. These are the expensive ones: a developer's node_modules is
# symlinks into a store that does not exist in the image, and dist would let a stale local
# bundle silently win over the one built here.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github

# Not part of the API bundle.
apps/web
!apps/web/package.json
apps/worker
!apps/worker/package.json
tests
**/test
docs
infra
logs
